# {{name}}

A game built on [Crucible](https://github.com/kryptic-sh/crcbl).

```sh
crcbl run                                  # open a window
crcbl run --headless -- --backend null     # no window, no driver; what CI runs
crcbl build --release
```

`--headless` is not a lesser mode: it is the same loop with `HeadlessShell` in
place of a window system, so a determinism check or a regression test needs no
display. `--backend null` drops the driver requirement too — the engine never
falls back to it on its own, because a game that silently rendered nothing
because a driver was missing would look like a black screen rather than an
error. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs that pair on every push.

## Layout

| Path          | What                                                                                           |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/main.rs` | The game: a `HostedGame` (simulation, input, HUD) and a `GameGpu` (renderers, render graph).   |
| `scenes/`     | Scene files. The format lands with `crcbl-scene`; the directory is here so the path is stable. |

The frame itself — pumping the shell, the fixed-timestep accumulator, the pause
menu, the debug overlay, presenting, teardown — is `crcbl::engine::Loop`. `ESC`,
`F11` and `F3` already work. `apps/bare` in the engine checkout is the other
shape, where the game writes the outer loop itself.

## The engine dependency

`Cargo.toml` points at a Crucible checkout by path, because the engine is not
published yet. Moving this project without moving the engine breaks the build;
fix it by editing that one path, or re-run `crcbl new --engine <checkout>`.
